    {
      "asset": {
        "kind": "figure",
        "key": "pone-0015338-g003",
        "anchor_key": "pone-0015338-g003",
        "heading": "Figure 3",
        "caption": "(A) Conventional contrast stretching transformation may be able to enhance the contrast of non-text regions as well as text regions; therefore, false localization can be anticipated. (B) We focused on only enhancing the contrast of text regions, not non-text regions. Our figure data presented that the gray-level of black text is usually lower than 10, and that of white text is higher than 230 in the 256 gray-level image. Therefore, we modified the contrast-stretching transformation by setting a<sub>1</sub> = 10 and a<sub>2</sub> = 230 to lower and raise the gray-level of black text and white text, respectively, while preserving the contrast of non-text regions.",
        "section": "body",
