        "heading": "Figure 5",
        "caption": "Three edit operations (i.e., two substitutions and one insertion) are required to transform “antlsnze” to “antisense”, while five edit operations (i.e., four substitutions and one insertion) are required to transform “antlsnze” to “antiserum”. Therefore, according to ED, “antisense” has a higher similarity than “antiserum” to the recognized form “antlsnze”.",
